new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d1182ee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/v1/multiprocess/DEEP_LOOKUP_ABLATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Deep-KV overhead, phase 1
+
+Only `LMCACHE_HYREX_PIPELINE_LOOKUP=1` changes behavior. Both independent
+LOOKUP submissions are sent before awaiting acknowledgements; both status
+queries are sent before awaiting their replies. Existing hit aggregation,
+cache-salt isolation, per-group locks, health handling and fallback remain.
+This overlaps RPC waiting, not GPU computation, and does not reduce RPC count.
+
+The standalone CPU check executes the actual adapter methods with fake futures.
+Run `python tests/v1/multiprocess/test_hyrex_lookup_pipeline_standalone.py`.
+It covers send-before-wait, 528/16 boundaries, pending/cached/missing results,
+multi-server inconsistent-hit lock release and submission timeout.
+
+The ABBA runner waits for native_tail_abba_20260928_v3 to complete before using
+GPU 1. Four identical 4-session, 10-turn passes compare flag 0/1/1/0 in eager
+mode with the frozen deep-KV model code, startup warmup and per-request GPU
+prefix clears. CPU LMCache persists between turns. Each pass starts a new
+service. First-token text, cache-hit lengths, reset success and formal JIT
+checks gate the result. These finite checks are not full numerical equivalence.
+
+Not implemented here: a combined wire-protocol lookup/retrieve, fused scatter,
+or Q-only normalization/RoPE changes. No TTFT gain is claimed before the run.
